  "answer": "The blue colour of the sky is due to a phenomenon called scattering of light. When sunlight enters Earth's atmosphere, it interacts with molecules like nitrogen and oxygen. These molecules are small and their size is comparable to the wavelength of blue light. As a result, blue light is scattered more than other colours in all directions. This scattered blue light reaches our eyes from all parts of the sky, making it appear blue. The scattering is more intense for shorter wavelengths, like blue, compared to longer wavelengths like red.",
